  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Mille Bornes. Logic: draw one per turn from stock; play one card (Roll, distance, remedy, safety, or hazard on opponent) or discard. Hand ends at target distance or when all cards played. Score by distance, safeties, coup-fourré, trip completion, and bonuses; game to 5000.',
    Player: 'Mille Bornes: draw one, play one or discard. Play Roll to drive, distance to advance, hazards on opponents, remedies and safeties on yourself. First to 1000 km wins the hand; first to 5000 points wins the game.',
    objective: 'Win a hand by being first to play enough distance cards to reach the target (1000 km in 4- or 6-player team play; 700 km in 2- or 3-player with option to extend to 1000). Win the game by being first to reach 5000 cumulative points.',
    gameplay: 'On your turn draw one card, then play one card or discard. Play Roll to drive; play distance cards (25–200 km) when Roll is showing; max two 200 km per hand. Play hazards on opponents; play remedies on your battle/speed area; play safeties for immunity and optional coup-fourré. Discard when no legal play. Hand ends when someone reaches target distance or all cards are played.',
    keyRules: [
      'Roll (Go) must show in your battle area before you can play distance cards; Right of Way safety waives this.',
      'Speed Limit limits you to 25 and 50 km distance until End of Limit is played.',
      'Each hazard has one remedy and one safety; safeties prevent that hazard for the rest of the hand.',
      'Coup-fourré: play the matching safety when an opponent plays the hazard against you; hazard is removed and you score 300 bonus.',
      'No more than two 200 km cards per player per hand; total distance cannot exceed target.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
